# Runtime appendix: React 19 (TSX)

The rules are in `00-zones.mdc`, `01-block-root.mdc`, `02-no-raw-html.mdc`,
`03-static-aria.mdc` and `06-fixtures-no-literal-text.mdc`. This file only maps
their terms to React 19 (TSX) syntax. Files: `*.tsx` inside the composition paths of the
packages whose `ui8kit.runtime` is `react` (see `rules/zones.json`).

## Paths

| Zone | Paths |
| --- | --- |
| Kit | `packages/kit/react` (UI8Kit 3 primitives); `packages/kit-compose/react/src/compose`, `src/icons`, `src/presets`, `src/utils`, `src/styles`; `apps/host-react/gen/runtime` |
| Composition | `packages/kit-compose/react/src/blocks`, `src/components`; `apps/host-react/gen/screens` |

## Syntax

| Term | Forbidden in composition | Use instead |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Raw HTML injection | `dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: markup }}` | kit components built from nodes |
| Dynamic tag | `createElement(tag, ...)`, `const Tag = cond ? "a" : "span"; <Tag/>` | a kit primitive with a `tag` prop |
| Raw native tag | `<div>`, `<span>`, `<svg>` and any lowercase JSX element | `Box`, `Text`, `Icon`, ... |
| Reactive ARIA state | `aria-expanded={open}` | a primitive prop: `<Button pressed={on}>` |
| Two-way binding | none in React (one-way `value` plus `onChange`) | |
| Literal text | `<Text>Save</Text>`, `label="Save"`, `{ok ? "Yes" : "No"}` | `{ui.group.key}`, `tpl(ui.group.key, { n })`, props |
| Component root | the first JSX element of the returned tree, looking through fragments, `&&`, `? :` and `.map()` | |
| One Block per file (rule 01) | two root-level `Block` in the same render path (siblings, a `Block` after `{a && ...}`); `Block` inside `.map` / `Array.from`; `Block` inside `Block` | each alternative of a ternary, `&&` / `\|\|` / `??` and each early return of the same component may hold its own single `Block`; any other second `Block` goes to a separate file |
| Block roots (rule 01) | a block or screen file that does not open on `Block`; `Nav`, `Figure`, `Article`, `Header`, `Footer`, `Blockquote` (removed) | any file may open on one `Block` with a semantic tag; a nested or looped `nav` / `figure` / `article` is a separate file rooted on `Block`; quotations and captions are `Text` with `tag` |

Allowed structure: `<>...</>`, `Fragment`, conditionals, `.map()`.
`createContext` / `useContext` are non-portable (`_nonportable.json`).
